### Did Donald Trump pay other forms of taxes, such as state income taxes, local property taxes, or federal payroll taxes, during the years he reportedly paid $750 in federal income taxes?
Answer: According to the search result, Donald Trump claimed that he "paid a lot of state income taxes too," specifically to New York state. Additionally, a lawyer for the Trump Organization stated that Trump had paid millions in "personal taxes" since 2015, which *The New York Times* noted "appeared to cover other federal taxes, including social security and Medicare."

Source URL: https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/27/new-york-times-publishes-donald-trumps-tax-returns-election

### During the September 26, 2016, presidential debate, did Donald Trump say "That makes me smart" in response to Hillary Clinton's assertion that Donald Trump paid zero federal income taxes in certain years?
Answer: Yes, during the debate, when Hillary Clinton suggested that Donald Trump paid no federal income tax for some years, Trump interjected, "That makes me smart." Although Trump later told reporters he "didn't say that at all," the search result confirms that he made the remark in response to Clinton's assertion.

Source URL: https://www.nbcnews.com/storyline/2016-presidential-debates/presidential-debate-donald-trump-s-remark-about-paying-taxes-raises-n655261

### Did Donald Trump make any public statements regarding his federal income tax payments between the publication of the New York Times report in September 2020 and Joe Biden's speech on October 30, 2020?
Answer: Yes, following the publication of the *New York Times* report on September 27, 2020, Donald Trump dismissed the findings as "fake news" during a Sunday evening news conference. When questioned about his federal income tax payments, Trump "refused to detail what he's paid in federal income taxes, saying simply: 'I've paid a lot,'" and asserted that "it'll all be revealed" once his tax returns are released after an audit.

