## Final Judgement
### Step 1: Summary of Key Insights
The retrieved evidence indicates that the *New York Times* reported Donald Trump paid $750 in federal income taxes in both 2016 and 2017, although he also paid other taxes, including state income taxes and federal payroll taxes (such as Social Security and Medicare). Regarding the quotes attributed to him, during a 2016 presidential debate, Trump did respond "That makes me smart" when Hillary Clinton asserted he paid no federal income taxes. However, the record does not show that Trump ever said "I know how to game the system."

### Step 2: Lacking Information
We are still lacking official transcripts or public records to verify whether Donald Trump ever uttered the phrase "I know how to game the system" in relation to his taxes. Without this information, we cannot fully verify the accuracy of the quote attributed to him by Joe Biden.

### Step 3: Conclusion
Based on the available evidence, the final decision is `not enough information`. While the $750 figure is documented regarding his federal income taxes (though omitting other taxes he paid), and his comment "That makes me smart" is verified, the lack of evidence regarding the second part of the quote ("I know how to game the system") prevents us from confirming or refuting the claim as a whole. Under the rules of this fact-check, the absence of evidence for this part of the claim means it remains unsupported.

### Verdict: NEI

### Justification
The final verdict is "not enough information" because key parts of the statement cannot be fully verified. While the [*New York Times*](https://www.vox.com/policy-and-politics/21459782/trump-750-tax-returns-nyt) reported that Donald Trump owed $750 in federal income taxes for 2016 and 2017, representatives noted he paid other personal, state, and payroll taxes during those years, as reported by [*The Guardian*](https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/27/new-york-times-publishes-donald-trumps-tax-returns-election). Furthermore, during a 2016 presidential debate, Trump did interject with "[That makes me smart](https://www.nbcnews.com/storyline/2016-presidential-debates/presidential-debate-donald-trump-s-remark-about-paying-taxes-raises-n655261)" when accused of paying zero federal income taxes. However, there is no evidence or public record confirming that Trump ever said, "I know how to game the system," leaving that portion of the quote unverified.